"health_atlas_cell_play_monocyte_1_caption" = "In response to local signals the cell moves toward a site where it can leave the vessel.";
"health_atlas_cell_play_monocyte_2_caption" = "It passes through the vessel lining and reaches the surrounding tissue.";
"health_atlas_cell_play_monocyte_3_caption" = "Some recruited monocytes become macrophages in the tissue. Not all macrophages come from this route.";
"health_atlas_cell_play_neutrophil_0_caption" = "Local signals guide the neutrophil toward the vessel wall.";
"health_atlas_cell_play_neutrophil_1_caption" = "The cell passes between cells of the vessel lining into the surrounding tissue.";
"health_atlas_cell_play_neutrophil_2_caption" = "It surrounds an encountered particle and encloses it in an internal compartment.";
"health_atlas_cell_play_neutrophil_3_caption" = "The cell brings granule contents to the compartment to help break down the material.";
"health_atlas_cell_play_nk_0_caption" = "A natural killer cell contacts neighboring cells and reads signals at their surfaces.";
"health_atlas_cell_play_nk_1_caption" = "A balance of activating and inhibitory signals helps it respond to an abnormal cell.";
"health_atlas_cell_play_nk_2_caption" = "It directs granule contents toward that cell at the point of contact.";
"health_atlas_cell_play_nk_3_caption" = "These contents can trigger a controlled cell-death process in the target cell.";
"health_atlas_cell_play_t_cell_0_caption" = "A T cell can recognize a matching fragment displayed by an antigen-presenting cell.";
"health_atlas_cell_play_t_cell_1_caption" = "Other activation signals help determine whether that T cell responds.";
"health_atlas_cell_play_t_cell_2_caption" = "Selected T cells divide, producing cells that recognize the same signal.";
"health_atlas_cell_play_t_cell_3_caption" = "The roles of T cells differ: some coordinate responses, some suppress them, and others act on target cells.";
