"health_atlas_endothelium_diffusion_caption" = "Small dissolved substances can diffuse across the lining in either direction. The net movement of each solute is from higher to lower concentration. This is not bulk fluid flow.";
"health_atlas_endothelium_drainage" = "Excess tissue fluid enters lymphatics";
"health_atlas_endothelium_drainage_caption" = "Excess fluid from the tissue space enters nearby lymphatic capillaries. Once inside, it is called lymph. This route does not depend on ongoing fluid uptake at the venous end of the blood capillary.";
"health_atlas_endothelium_filtration" = "Some water filters out";
"health_atlas_endothelium_filtration_caption" = "In many tissues, the balance of pressures lets some water filter from the blood into the tissue space. This outward flow is called filtration.";
