"health_atlas_placental_exchange_story_gases_caption" = "Oxygen moves overall from maternal blood to fetal blood; carbon dioxide moves overall in the opposite direction. They diffuse across the thin villous barrier down their respective partial-pressure gradients. The arrows show net transfer of gases, not the motion of blood cells.";
