"health_atlas_placental_exchange_story_interface_caption" = "The syncytiotrophoblast is a continuous outer layer with many nuclei that is in direct contact with maternal blood. Fetal blood remains within the capillary endothelium. Where the capillary hugs the surface, very little tissue separates the blood streams.";
