"health_atlas_placental_exchange_story_nutrients_caption" = "Glucose is one example of a nutrient that moves overall toward fetal blood. GLUT1 proteins on both sides of the syncytiotrophoblast help glucose cross that layer by facilitated diffusion. Different nutrients can use different mechanisms.";
"health_atlas_placental_exchange_story_orient" = "Find the exchange surface";
"health_atlas_placental_exchange_story_orient_caption" = "The placenta lies against the uterine wall and connects to the fetus through the umbilical cord. On the fetal side, trees of chorionic villi branch into a space filled with maternal blood. The ring marks one of the fine tips, called terminal villi.";
