"health_atlas_placental_exchange_story_routes_caption" = "Maternal blood enters through uterine spiral arteries, flows around the villi in the intervillous space, and drains into uterine veins. Two umbilical arteries bring fetal blood to the villous capillaries; one umbilical vein returns it to the fetus. The two blood streams do not directly mix during normal exchange.";
